            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0447" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.5124/19.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Denmark to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Denmark</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to the
                    memorandum of the Department of State addressed to this Legation on February
                    7th, 1912, with regard to the interpretation of Article 7 of the Treaty between
                    Denmark and the United States of April 26th, 1826, I beg to state that the
                    question of the rate of the inheritance tax on the estate of the late Ane
                    Margrethe Andersen having been decided against the heirs in the District Court
                    of Iowa, the case will be appealed, on behalf of the said heirs, to the Supreme
                    Court of the State of Iowa.</p>
                <p>I am directed by my Government to ascertain whether, in case the decision of the
                    Supreme Court of Iowa should also go against the heirs, an appeal to the Supreme
                    Court of the United States would be possible, and I should feel greatly obliged
                    to your excellency for submitting this question to the competent official and
                    informing me of his reply.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.].</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Brun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
